{{Term/Store|Flurry Rush|Flurry Rushes|Series, BotW, TotK, AoI|plural}} are recurring abilities in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Game Screen"/><ref name="TotK Game Screen"/><ref name="AoI Game Screen"/>{{Name Ref|AoC}}

==Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Stub|BotW}}
[[Link]] can perform a Flurry Rush in {{BotW}} after he successfully performs a [[Perfect Dodging|Perfect Dodge]]. According to "[[Daruk's Training Journal]]", Flurry Rush is a result of Link's intense focus making it seem as if [[Time]] has slowed down from his perspective.<ref name="BotW Daruk's Training Journal"/> While focusing, Link is capable of performing multiple hits in quick succession with his [[Weapon]] in a short period of time. If Link does not hit the [[Enemy]] within a certain period of time after initiating the Flurry Rush, it will cancel, and the flow of time will normalize.

==={{TotK|-}}===
The Flurry Rush returns in {{TotK}}, retaining its characteristics from {{BotW}}. However, [[Demon King Ganondorf]] can also use the Flurry Rush ability against Link in his boss battle, requiring the latter to use the ability twice in a row to counter him.

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Stub|AoC}}
Flurry Rush is an ability [[Warrior]]s can use in {{AoC}} to deal damage to the exposed [[Weak Point Gauge]]s of powerful [[Enemy|Enemies]] and [[Boss]]es.
{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{AoI|-}}===
Flurry Rushes return in {{AoI}}, allowing [[Warrior]]s to dodge [[Enemy]] attacks and deplete an Enemy's [[Weak Point Gauge]].

